1474..1547 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1548..1605 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1606..1677 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1678..1754 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1755..1831 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
1832..1906 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
1907..1985 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
1986..2028 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
2029..2031 Other "@["
2032..2040 Other "respects"
